BManx2000 schrieb:
> Marcel Bollmann wrote:
>> Having said that, the script gives me an error in Windows because the 
>> "getpwuid" call isn't implemented (latest ActivePerl release). If I 
>> replace it, everything runs fine.
> 
> Could you explain what you did to fix that? I have the same ActivePerl 
> release (thank you, Google) and I get the same error, but I know nothing 
> about this stuff.

I replaced all occurrences of "getpwuid(...)" (ie. regardless what's 
between the round brackets) with an empty string. The quickest way to do 
that is via the command line - change to the directory with the 
loghack.pl file and enter:

   perl -p -i.bak -e "s/getpwuid\(.*?\)/\"\"/g" loghack.pl

I don't know if there's a better way around this problem, but at least 
this works.

